<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul frees interest on stock customer deposits.</title>
<headline>Seoul frees interest on stock customer deposits.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Securities and Exchange Commission said the liberalisation of interest on customer deposits at brokerage houses to up to five percent a year took effect from the start of Wednesday.</p>
<p>Earlier the rate was fixed at three percent annually.  </p>
<p>The Finance and Economy Ministry announced on Monday it would liberalise interest rates on such deposits as part of a plan to boost the sagging stock market.</p>
<p>At that time the ministry said the timing of the liberalisation would be announced later.</p>
<p>A statement from the commission said from Wednesday brokerages could set interest rates on the customer deposits up to five percent.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5646</p>
